              o.type in ['', 'container_t', 'container_init_t', 'container_kvm_t', 'container_engine_t']))
          message: securityContext.seLinuxOptions.type (pod and containers[*]) must be unset or one of container_t, container_init_t, container_kvm_t, container_engine_t. If this workload needs another type, add a posture exception for restrict-selinux.
        - expression: |-
            variables.exempt || (variables.seLinuxOptions.all(o,
              (!has(o.user) || o.user == '') && (!has(o.role) || o.role == '')))
          message: securityContext.seLinuxOptions.user and .role (pod and containers[*]) must be unset. If this workload needs them, add a posture exception for restrict-selinux.
      variables:
        - expression: 'object.kind == ''Pod'' ? object.spec : (object.kind == ''CronJob'' ? object.spec.jobTemplate.spec.template.spec : object.spec.template.spec)'
          name: podSpec
